codex
The first symbolic attempt exposed a K backend performance trap: simplifying nested hooked `replaceAll` operations over an unknown string consumed CPU before even reaching depth 3. I’ve isolated that hook behind a semantics primitive whose defining rule is marked concrete. Concrete `krun` still computes real replacements, while symbolic proof compares the program and contract as identical character-deletion operations without forcing the backend to solve an opaque arbitrary-string replacement.
apply patch
